{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1202917-2e-npc-guardian-seer-double-agent-mentor","id":1202917,"title":"[2E] [NPC] Guardian/Seer double Agent Mentor","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-04T02:12:39-07:00","id":1202917,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> [2E] [NPC] Guardian/Seer double Agent Mentor","content":"Hi, guys. I am about to start a new chronicle and want to set the plot-twist from the start. Thus I need help fleshing out the main NPC. Point is I don't know if I'm crunching the mechanics the right way. Anyway, here is the basic seed.<br /> <br /> -Meet a retired Guardian Acanthus, now a Master of Fate, who long ago infiltrated a Seers of the Throne pylon by building a Seer Persona through his Mask. <br /> -In fact he was so good at it, that he became a Prelate.<br /> -But the things they made him do, drove him nuts and he became one of the Mad with obsession to constantly seek the Exarch's Will.<br /> -To save his sanity, he restricted his &quot;craziness&quot; to his Seer Persona through his Mask.<br /> -Due to Coincidences and Madness, he eradicated all that knew about the specifics of his double-agent status both Seers and Pentacle. But was excommunicated from both.<br /> -His few current associates know that he was once a double-agent but consider his Mad persona a different person. He has still some connections to both factions.<br /> -To this day he periodically summons &quot;Inner Destiny&quot;, a specific Moira of Fate and Mind to contain his Mad Persona from taking control.<br /> -Unknown to him, his Seer Persona also summons a Supernal Entity to break from her prison.<br /> <br /> Some questions<br /> -Is it possible to separate the Madness and the Prelacy from the main persona with just the Mask merit? If not how could I use that idea within the mechanics?<br /> -Can the Persona have different Arcana than the main one (so that she can summon different kind of Supernal Entity)? It would be a giveaway if both personas use Entities of the same path.<br /> -How can the persona summon entities if she is contained within the Oneiros?<br /> -What would be a linear progression of Mysteries that would lead to uncovering the plot-twist and what the resolution?<br /> <br /> The main reason I want the Mad Persona to summon Supernal Entities is as means for her to interact with my PCs. The first chapter would be the player characters investigating about the after-effects of the Mad's Supernal Entity and maybe connect her with the Nimbus of a Mad One (which would be different than their Mentor's).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","name":"Shadowjim12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T03:16:32-07:00","id":1202930,"title":"","content":"If a PC did it then no, this would never work, Madness is having a fractured soul not just an unstable personality. Fortunately, we\u2019re talking NPC, so yeah it totally works.<br /> <br /> They have to have the same arcana, but that doesn\u2019t mean they have to use all of them. Say he knows four arcana, just decide that each personality only uses two.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s an NPC, you can hand wave it, also the Mad generate Tulpas naturally to try to force the Mad to indulge in his Madness when they are showing more discipline. If the main personality is ignoring his Madness those Tulpas are going to do things in the real world to try to force him to release it, and if it takes summoning a Supernal Entity then that\u2019s what it takes.<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t write your plot for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T03:47:58-07:00","id":1202936,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> I'm asking because I'm not sure how do keep consistent with the rules and how to present him without alerting my players too much. But you are right, it was too generic a question. Let me break it down to more specific ones. These are the main questions that concern me at the moment<br /> <br /> a) I remember reading that Mages can't summon Entities from different paths. Since his &quot;Sane&quot; Personality summons Moirae could his &quot;Mad&quot; Personality summon (Seer-related) Cherubim?<br /> b) Can Tulpas manifest as phenomena or is the mage compelled to cast them by spending his own actions?<br /> c) Would a focused Mind Mage Sight or an Oneiros Astral Journey immediately reveal someone as Mad or Prelate?<br /> d) Can mages trace the nimbus of the summoner from a Supernal Entity he summoned?<br /> <br /> Please excuse my lack of creativity. It is trapped in a potential well at the moment <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","name":"Shadowjim12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T04:07:10-07:00","id":1202939,"title":"","content":"A) They can\u2019t summon entities of different Paths, but if the Mad part of him is trapped in his Oneiros he might be capable of using the Prelacy gate in there to summon Ochemata from the Exarchs which would reflect the arcana of the Exarch he unwillingly serves, which could be the General or whatever the Prime one was.<br /> <br /> B) Tulpas aren\u2019t exactly spells or creatures and don\u2019t take actions, they\u2019re magical effects created by the metaphysical fallout that leaks from the Fault in a Mad ones soul. Maybe the best way to think of them are as extreme manifestations of Long Term Nimbus.<br /> <br /> C) An Oneiros Astral Journey certainly could if they get into the part of the Oneiros where the Fault or the Gate manifest.<br /> <br /> D) Probably not, unless they trace the entity back to where it was summoned from, they probably can pick it up from there because the entity is probably summoned in a Sanctum or demesne regularly used by the summoner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 04-04-2018, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T04:44:46-07:00","id":1202948,"title":"","content":"Thanks, man. That helped alot <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","name":"Shadowjim12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T08:50:07-07:00","id":1203026,"title":"","content":"If they have a Mind Legacy, one of the Attainments might be able to create Goetia and/or new intelligences. That would give you a mechanical base for their Tulpa and Mad Persona to act separate from the Guardian one. As Legacy Attainments, they are also harder to disperse magically. Prime and Death can hide any tell-tale Nimbus markings to obfuscate who they belong to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T09:16:48-07:00","id":1203040,"title":"","content":"Prelacies are granted by the Exarchs, and I have difficulty imagining a 'normal' mage managing to fool them with nothing but a Mask and non-Imperial magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T10:18:22-07:00","id":1203054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1202917-2e-npc-guardian-seer-double-agent-mentor?p=1203040#post1203040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prelacies are granted by the Exarchs, and I have difficulty imagining a 'normal' mage managing to fool them with nothing but a Mask and non-Imperial magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt they\u2019d care. A Mage foolish enough to make the commitment of opening a Gate to them is a Mage that they have more directly under their thumb than anyone else, even if they\u2019re attempting subversion or rebellion against the Exarchs. To care would be to acknowledge they can be threatened, and you have to accomplish some pretty horrific stuff before they build that Gate in your Oneiros in the first place, things which further their goals. It\u2019s basically win/win for the Exarchs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T10:24:09-07:00","id":1203056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1202917-2e-npc-guardian-seer-double-agent-mentor?p=1203054#post1203054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I doubt they\u2019d care. A Mage foolish enough to make the commitment of opening a Gate to them is a Mage that they have more directly under their thumb than anyone else, even if they\u2019re attempting subversion or rebellion against the Exarchs. To care would be to acknowledge they can be threatened, and you have to accomplish some pretty horrific stuff before they build that Gate in your Oneiros in the first place, things which further their goals. It\u2019s basically win/win for the Exarchs.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a really good point, actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T11:18:38-07:00","id":1203072,"title":"","content":"I believe Signs of Sorcery is supposed to go into what happens to pentacle mages when they call upon the Exarchs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T11:40:50-07:00","id":1203079,"title":"","content":"There's a Condition for &quot;was a big enough of an idiot to use an Exarch as a Yantra without first being a Seer&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T02:05:40-07:00","id":1203764,"title":"","content":"Damn, I so wish to have that book in my hands <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11688-marciano666","name":"marciano666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}